                <name>DEV_DYNAMIC_ADDR</name>
                <description>Device Dynamic Address with parity. 

This field consists of a Dynamic Address and a Parity Bit.
The LSBs [22:16] consist of the Dynamic Address to be assigned for the winning I3C device when using ENTDAA command.
The MSB [23] is the odd parity of the 7-bit Dynamic Address used for ENTDAA address assignment (~XOR(DEV_DYNAMIC_ADDR[22:16])</description>
                <bitRange>[23:16]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>DEV_NACK_RETRY_CNT</name>
                <description>This field is used to set the Device NACK Retry count for the particular device.

If the Device NACKs for the device address, the block automatically retries the transfer until this count expires.
If the Target NACKs for the mentioned number of retries, then the block generates an error response and moves to the Halt state.

This feature is used for Retry Model for the following features mentioned in the I3C Specification:
=&gt; Retry Model for Direct GET CCC Commands
=&gt; The incoming TIR-IBI matches with the Target address initated by the Active Controller</description>
                <bitRange>[30:29]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>LEGACY_I2C_DEVICE</name>
