          <register>
            <name>TR_SAMPLE_TIME</name>
            <description>SAR Trigger Sample Time (Risk Mitigation Only)</description>
            <addressOffset>0x18</addressOffset>
            <size>32</size>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x5001F</resetValue>
            <resetMask>0x3FF03FF</resetMask>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>HS_TR_SAMPLE_TIME</name>
                <description>High Speed (HS) Trigger Sample Time

This field is for risk mitigation purposes only.

This field is only applicable if TR_SAMPLE_TIME_EN is set by the Entry Address pointed to by the Autonomous Controller. HS_TR_SAMPLE_TIME sets the number of HS clock cycles to allow for sampling of the first address (Entry Address) of a scan.

Entry Address Sample Time  = HS_TR_SAMPLE_TIME+1, range 1..1024</description>
                <bitRange>[9:0]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>LP_TR_SAMPLE_TIME</name>
                <description>Low Power (LP) Trigger Sample Time

This field is for risk mitigation purposes only.

This field is only applicable if TR_SAMPLE_TIME_EN is set by the Entry Address pointed to by the Autonomous Controller. LP_TR_SAMPLE_TIME sets the number of LP clock cycles to allow for sampling.

Entry Address Sample Time  = LP_TR_SAMPLE_TIME+1, range 1..1024</description>
                <bitRange>[25:16]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <dim>4</dim>
            <dimIncrement>4</dimIncrement>
            <name>SAMPLE_TIME[%s]</name>
            <description>Sample control register (only accessible if ACTRLR.STATUS.MODE=0)</description>
            <addressOffset>0x20</addressOffset>
            <size>32</size>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x5001F</resetValue>
            <resetMask>0x3FF03FF</resetMask>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>HS_SAMPLE_TIME</name>
                <description>Sample time (aperture) in HS clock cycles (nominally 80MHz). 
Sample time = SAMPLE_TIME+1, range 1..1024</description>
                <bitRange>[9:0]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>LP_SAMPLE_TIME</name>
                <description>Sample time (aperture) in LP clock cycles (4MHz). 
Sample time = SAMPLE_TIME+1, range 1..1024</description>
                <bitRange>[25:16]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
            </fields>
