            <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
            <resetMask>0x0</resetMask>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>SAR_ENTRY_ADDR</name>
                <description>SAR Timer Table Entry State

This field is a pointer to the entry address of the SAR sequencer state table.

If ACTRLR.STATUS.MODE=0, this field points to the High Speed state table (SEQ.HS.DATA)
If ACTRLR.STATUS.MODE=1, this field points to the Low Power state table (SEQ.LP.DATA)

Valid values are 0-31.

This field is ignored unless the following conditions are guaranteed:

1.  The SAR is triggered (SAR_TR=1).
2.  The SAR has been enabled in a prior state (SAR_EN=1) and is ready (i.e. the AC has waited for BLOCK_READY in the same state where the SAR was enabled).
3.  The SAR is idle (SAR.SAR_STA_CFG.STATUS.BUSY=0).

This field is pointer to the entry address of the SAR sequencer state table.

If ACTRLR.STATUS.MODE=0, this field points to the High Speed state table (SEQ.HS.DATA)
If ACTRLR.STATUS.MODE=1, this field points to the Low Power state table (SEQ.LP.DATA)</description>
                <bitRange>[4:0]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>RSVD_2</name>
                <description>N/A</description>
                <bitRange>[5:5]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>SAR_TR</name>
                <description>SAR Trigger (initiate SAR operation at sequencer address pointed to by SAR_ENTRY_ADDR)

When entering a state where this field is set, the AC generates a single cycle pulse (trigger) to the SAR sequencer. This trigger is ignored by the SAR sequencer unless ALL of the following conditions are guaranteed:

1.  The SAR has been enabled in a prior state (SAR_EN=1) and is ready (i.e. the AC has waited for BLOCK_READY in the same state where the SAR was enabled).
2.  The SAR is idle (SAR.SAR_STA_CFG.STATUS.BUSY=0).</description>
                <bitRange>[6:6]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>SAR_EN</name>
                <description>SAR enable

This field is only used by the Autonomous Controller if SAR_UNLOCK is set.  Otherwise, the field is ignored.</description>
                <bitRange>[7:7]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>DISABLED</name>
                    <description>Disabled</description>
                    <value>0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>ENABLED</name>
                    <description>Enabled

SAR is powered and all SAR (FIR) logic is enabled and clocked.</description>
                    <value>1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>DAC0_CHANNEL</name>
                <description>DAC0 Channel select

This field is pointer to the active DAC channel.  Valid values are 0-15.

This field is ignored unless the following conditions are guaranteed:

1.  The DAC is triggered (DAC0_TR=1).
2.  The DAC has been enabled in a prior state (DAC0_EN=1) and is ready (i.e. the AC has waited for BLOCK_READY in the same state where DAC0 was enabled).</description>
                <bitRange>[11:8]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CHANNEL_0</name>
                    <description>Channel 0 </description>
                    <value>0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CHANNEL_1</name>
                    <description>Channel 1 </description>
                    <value>1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CHANNEL_2</name>
                    <description>Channel 2 </description>
                    <value>2</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CHANNEL_3</name>
                    <description>Channel 3 </description>
                    <value>3</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CHANNEL_4</name>
                    <description>Channel 4 </description>
                    <value>4</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CHANNEL_5</name>
                    <description>Channel 5 </description>
                    <value>5</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CHANNEL_6</name>
                    <description>Channel 6 </description>
                    <value>6</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CHANNEL_7</name>
                    <description>Channel 7 </description>
                    <value>7</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CHANNEL_8</name>
                    <description>Channel 8 </description>
                    <value>8</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CHANNEL_9</name>
                    <description>Channel 9 </description>
                    <value>9</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CHANNEL_10</name>
                    <description>Channel 10 </description>
                    <value>10</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CHANNEL_11</name>
                    <description>Channel 11 </description>
                    <value>11</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CHANNEL_12</name>
                    <description>Channel 12 </description>
                    <value>12</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CHANNEL_13</name>
                    <description>Channel 13</description>
                    <value>13</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CHANNEL_14</name>
                    <description>Channel 14 </description>
                    <value>14</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>FW_CHANNEL</name>
                    <description>FW Channel</description>
                    <value>15</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>DAC0_TR</name>
                <description>DAC0 Trigger

This field initiates DAC operation per the DAC0_CHANNEL selection.  When entering a state where this field is set, the AC generates a single cycle pulse (trigger) to the DAC0 logic.

This field is ignored unless: the DAC has been enabled in a prior state (DAC0_EN=1) and is ready (i.e. the AC has waited for BLOCK_READY in the same state where DAC0 was enabled).

The DAC does NOT need to be disabled when switching channels.</description>
                <bitRange>[12:12]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>DAC0_INC</name>
                <description>DAC0 Increment

When entering a state where this field is set, the AC generates a single cycle pulse (increment) to the DAC0 logic.

DAC_INC and DAC_DEC CANNOT be simultaneously set in a given state (doing so will cause DAC_DEC to be ignored by the DAC0 logic).

This field is only used by the DAC0 logic if the DAC0_CHANNEL field is set to 0-14 (Hardware channels) and DAC0.DAC_STA_CFG.CHAN_CFG.MODE = ADDR or DATA.

If DAC0.DAC_STA_CFG.CHAN_CFG.MODE=ADDR, the DAC0 logic increments the DAC address (Amount set by DAC0.DAC_STA_CFG.CHAN_CFG.STEP_SIZE_EN and STEP_SIZE_SEL)

If DAC0.DAC_STA_CFG.CHAN_CFG.MODE=DATA, the DAC0 logic increments the DAC Value (Amount set by CHAN_CFG.STEP_SIZE_EN and STEP_SIZE_SEL)</description>
                <bitRange>[13:13]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>DAC0_DEC</name>
                <description>DAC0 Decrement

When entering a state where this field is set, the AC generates a single cycle pulse (decrement) to the DAC0 logic.

DAC_INC and DAC_DEC CANNOT be simultaneously set in a given state (doing so will cause DAC_DEC to be ignored by the DAC0 logic).

This field is only used by the DAC0 logic if the DAC0_CHANNEL field is set to 0-14 (Hardware channels) and DAC0.DAC_STA_CFG.CHAN_CFG.MODE = ADDR or DATA.

If DAC0.DAC_STA_CFG.CHAN_CFG.MODE=ADDR, the DAC0 logic decrements the DAC address (Amount set by DAC0.DAC_STA_CFG.CHAN_CFG.STEP_SIZE_EN and STEP_SIZE_SEL)

If DAC0.DAC_STA_CFG.CHAN_CFG.MODE=DATA, the DAC0 logic decrements the DAC Value (Amount set by CHAN_CFG.STEP_SIZE_EN and STEP_SIZE_SEL)</description>
                <bitRange>[14:14]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>DAC0_EN</name>
                <description>DAC0 enable

This field is only used by the Autonomous Controller if DAC0_UNLOCK is set.  Otherwise, the field is ignored.</description>
                <bitRange>[15:15]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>DISABLED</name>
                    <description>Disabled

DAC0 is powered down, DAC0 logic is reset, DAC0 clocks are gated,  and all DAC0 AC conditions are cleared.  DAC0 configuration and waveform tables are retained.</description>
                    <value>0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>ENABLED</name>
                    <description>Enabled

DAC0 is powered and all logic is enabled and clocked.</description>
                    <value>1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>DAC1_CHANNEL</name>
                <description>See DAC0_CHANNEL</description>
                <bitRange>[19:16]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>DAC1_TR</name>
                <description>See DAC0_TR</description>
                <bitRange>[20:20]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>DAC1_INC</name>
                <description>See DAC0_INC</description>
                <bitRange>[21:21]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>DAC1_DEC</name>
                <description>See DAC0_DEC</description>
                <bitRange>[22:22]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>DAC1_EN</name>
                <description>See DAC0_EN</description>
                <bitRange>[23:23]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>PTC_CMP0_CFG</name>
                <description>PTC Comp0 Mux Configuration

This field determines the state of all input muxes to the Comparator 0.

This field is only used by the Autonomous Controller if PTC_UNLOCK is set.  Otherwise, the field is ignored.</description>
                <bitRange>[26:24]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CFG_0</name>
                    <description>Configuration 0 

Mux settings determined by PTC_DYN_CFG_STRUCT_Regs0</description>
                    <value>0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CFG_1</name>
                    <description>Configuration 1 

Mux settings determined by PTC_DYN_CFG_STRUCT_Regs1</description>
                    <value>1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CFG_2</name>
                    <description>Configuration 2 

Mux settings determined by PTC_DYN_CFG_STRUCT_Regs2</description>
                    <value>2</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CFG_3</name>
                    <description>Configuration 3 

Mux settings determined by PTC_DYN_CFG_STRUCT_Regs3</description>
                    <value>3</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CFG_4</name>
                    <description>Configuration 4 

Mux settings determined by PTC_DYN_CFG_STRUCT_Regs4</description>
                    <value>4</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CFG_5</name>
                    <description>Configuration 5 

Mux settings determined by PTC_DYN_CFG_STRUCT_Regs5</description>
                    <value>5</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CFG_6</name>
                    <description>Configuration 6 

Mux settings determined by PTC_DYN_CFG_STRUCT_Regs6</description>
                    <value>6</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>CFG_7</name>
                    <description>Configuration 7 

Mux settings determined by PTC_DYN_CFG_STRUCT_Regs7</description>
                    <value>7</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>PTC_CMP0_EN</name>
                <description>PTC Comparator0 enable

This field is only used by the Autonomous Controller if PTC_UNLOCK is set.  Otherwise, the field is ignored.</description>
                <bitRange>[27:27]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>DISABLED</name>
                    <description>Disabled

PTC Comparator 0 is powered down, Comparator 0 logic is reset, and Comparator 0 clock is gated.  PTC_COMP0 AC condition is cleared.  PTC_STROBE0 and PTC_RANGE0 are functional if PTC_COMP1_EN is set.  Otherwise those conditions are cleared/disabled.   PTC Comparator 0 configuration is retained.</description>
                    <value>0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>ENABLED</name>
                    <description>Enabled

PTC Comparator 0 is powered and all logic is enabled and clocked.</description>
                    <value>1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>PTC_CMP1_CFG</name>
                <description>See PTC_CMP0_CFG</description>
                <bitRange>[30:28]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>PTC_CMP1_EN</name>
                <description>See PTC_CMP0_EN</description>
                <bitRange>[31:31]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>TT_CFG4</name>
            <description>AC Table Configuration 4</description>
            <addressOffset>0x10</addressOffset>
            <size>32</size>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
            <resetMask>0x8F8F0000</resetMask>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>PRB_VREF0_VAL</name>
                <description>TAP location for PRB VREF0.

This field is only used by the Autonomous Controller if PRB_UNLOCK is set.  Otherwise, the field is ignored.

Prior the writing to this field, the following must be met:

1.  PRB.VREF_CTRL0.EN=1 (VREF0 is enabled)
2.  PRB_VREF0_FW_MODE = 0 (VREF0 is configured for Autonomous Controller control)

The field is reset only when disabling the AC.</description>
                <bitRange>[19:16]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>TAP_0</name>
                    <description>VREF0 = 0.06*PRB.VREF_CTRL.CFG</description>
                    <value>0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>TAP_1</name>
                    <description>VREF0 = 0.13*PRB.VREF_CTRL.CFG</description>
                    <value>1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>TAP_2</name>
                    <description>VREF0 = 0.19*PRB.VREF_CTRL.CFG</description>
                    <value>2</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>TAP_3</name>
                    <description>VREF0 = 0.25*PRB.VREF_CTRL.CFG</description>
                    <value>3</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>TAP_4</name>
                    <description>VREF0 = 0.31*PRB.VREF_CTRL.CFG</description>
                    <value>4</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>TAP_5</name>
                    <description>VREF0 = 0.38*PRB.VREF_CTRL.CFG</description>
                    <value>5</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>TAP_6</name>
                    <description>VREF0 = 0.44*PRB.VREF_CTRL.CFG</description>
                    <value>6</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>TAP_7</name>
                    <description>VREF0 = 0.50*PRB.VREF_CTRL.CFG</description>
                    <value>7</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>TAP_8</name>
                    <description>VREF0 = 0.56*PRB.VREF_CTRL.CFG</description>
                    <value>8</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>TAP_9</name>
                    <description>VREF0 = 0.63*PRB.VREF_CTRL.CFG</description>
                    <value>9</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>TAP_10</name>
                    <description>VREF0 = 0.69*PRB.VREF_CTRL.CFG</description>
                    <value>10</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>TAP_11</name>
                    <description>VREF0 = 0.75*PRB.VREF_CTRL.CFG</description>
                    <value>11</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>TAP_12</name>
                    <description>VREF0 = 0.81*PRB.VREF_CTRL.CFG</description>
                    <value>12</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>TAP_13</name>
                    <description>VREF0 = 0.88*PRB.VREF_CTRL.CFG</description>
                    <value>13</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>TAP_14</name>
                    <description>VREF0 = 0.94*PRB.VREF_CTRL.CFG</description>
                    <value>14</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>TAP_15</name>
                    <description>VREF0 = 1.00*PRB.VREF_CTRL.CFG</description>
                    <value>15</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>PRB_VREF0_FW_MODE</name>
                <description>PRB VREF0 Firmware Mode

This field is only used by the Autonomous Controller if PRB_UNLOCK is set.  Otherwise, the field is ignored.

Prior to writing to this field, VREF0 must be enabled (PRB.VREF_CTRL0.EN=1).</description>
                <bitRange>[23:23]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>DISABLED</name>
                    <description>Disabled (PRB output determined by TT.CFG4.PRB_VREF0_VAL)</description>
                    <value>0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>ENABLED</name>
                    <description>Enabled (PRB output determined by PRB.PRB_VREF_CTRL0.VAL)</description>
                    <value>1</value>
