              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>DAC1_RANGE0</name>
              <description>DAC1 Range 0 Trigger

It is generated by the DAC1 if the RANGE0 condition is met for a given channel with range 0 status enabled (i.e. DAC1_STA_CFG.CHAN_CFG.STATUS_SEL=STATUS_0).  The interrupt is disabled when DAC1 is configured for FW mode.</description>
              <bitRange>[13:13]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>DAC1_RANGE1</name>
              <description>DAC1 Range 1 Trigger

It is generated by the DAC1 if the RANGE1 condition is met for a given channel with range 1 status enabled (i.e. DAC1_STA_CFG.CHAN_CFG.STATUS_SEL=STATUS_1).  The interrupt is disabled when DAC1 is configured for FW mode.</description>
              <bitRange>[14:14]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>DAC1_RANGE2</name>
              <description>DAC1 Range 2 Trigger

It is generated by the DAC1 if the RANGE2 condition is met for a given channel with range 2 status enabled (i.e. DAC1_STA_CFG.CHAN_CFG.STATUS_SEL=STATUS_2).  The interrupt is disabled when DAC1 is configured for FW mode.</description>
              <bitRange>[15:15]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>DAC1_EPOCH</name>
              <description>DAC1 End of Waveform Trigger

It is generated by DAC1 when finishing a waveform.  This condition is only used if the DAC1 channel (pointed to by the AC when triggered) is configured for LUT mode.</description>
              <bitRange>[16:16]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_LEVEL0</name>
              <description>FIFO Level 0 Trigger

This is a level sensitive trigger that is generated by the FIFO whenever FIFO 0 meets the FIFO_STA_CFG.LEVEL0.LEVEL condition.</description>
              <bitRange>[17:17]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SAR_DONE</name>
              <description>SAR Sequencer Done Trigger

This trigger is set by the SAR when finishing a state in the SAR sequencer table (HS or LP) where SAR.SEQ_HS(LP)_DATA.NEXT_STATE is set to STOP.  The interrupt is not generated if the SAR is configured for CONTINUOUS operation (i.e. SAR.SEQ_HS(LP)_DATA.NEXT_STATE is set to GO_TO_ENTRY_ADDRESS).  

This trigger does NOT indicate that the SAR data has been written to the FIFO (the FIFO level triggers should be used instead).</description>
              <bitRange>[18:18]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SAR_EOS</name>
              <description>SAR Sequencer EOS Trigger

This itrigger is set by the SAR when finishing the state in the SAR sequencer table (HS or LP) where SAR.SEQ_HS(LP)_DATA.NEXT_STATE is set to GO_TO_ENTRY_ADDRESS or STOP.  

This trigger does NOT indicate that the SAR data has been written to the FIFO (the FIFO level triggers should be used instead).</description>
              <bitRange>[19:19]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_LEVEL1</name>
              <description>FIFO Level 1 Trigger

This level sensitive trigger is generated by the FIFO whenever FIFO 1 meets the FIFO_STA_CFG.LEVEL1.LEVEL condition.

This trigger is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=1,2, or 3)</description>
              <bitRange>[20:20]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SAR_RANGE0</name>
              <description>SAR Range 0 Trigger

This trigger is set by the SAR if the RANGE0 condition is met for a given channel with range 0 status enabled (i.e. SAR_STA_CFG.GPIO(MUX)_CHAN_CFG.STATUS_SEL=STATUS_STRUCT_0).   Firmware must read SAR_STA_CFG.RANGE_STATUS to determine which channel generated the trigger.</description>
              <bitRange>[21:21]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SAR_RANGE1</name>
              <description>SAR Range 1 Trigger

This trigger is set by the SAR if the RANGE1 condition is met for a given channel with range 1 status enabled (i.e. SAR_STA_CFG.GPIO(MUX)_CHAN_CFG.STATUS_SEL=STATUS_STRUCT_1).   Firmware must read SAR_STA_CFG.RANGE_STATUS to determine which channel generated the trigger.</description>
              <bitRange>[22:22]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SAR_RANGE2</name>
              <description>SAR Range 2 Trigger

This trigger is set by the SAR if the RANGE2 condition is met for a given channel with range 2 status enabled (i.e. SAR_STA_CFG.GPIO(MUX)_CHAN_CFG.STATUS_SEL=STATUS_STRUCT_2).   Firmware must read SAR_STA_CFG.RANGE_STATUS to determine which channel generated the trigger.</description>
              <bitRange>[23:23]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SAR_RANGE3</name>
              <description>SAR Range 3 Trigger

This trigger is set by the SAR if the RANGE3 condition is met for a given channel with range 3 status enabled (i.e. SAR_STA_CFG.GPIO(MUX)_CHAN_CFG.STATUS_SEL=STATUS_STRUCT_3).   Firmware must read SAR_STA_CFG.RANGE_STATUS to determine which channel generated the trigger.</description>
              <bitRange>[24:24]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_LEVEL2</name>
              <description>FIFO Level 2 Trigger

This level sensitive trigger is set by the FIFO whenever FIFO 2 meets the FIFO_STA_CFG.LEVEL2.LEVEL condition.

This trigger is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=2, or 3)</description>
              <bitRange>[25:25]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_LEVEL3</name>
              <description>FIFO Level 3 Trigger

This level sensitive trigger is set by the FIFO whenever FIFO 3 meets the FIFO_STA_CFG.LEVEL3.LEVEL condition.

This trigger is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=2, or 3)</description>
              <bitRange>[26:26]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_LEVEL4</name>
              <description>FIFO Level 4 Trigger

This level sensitive trigger is set by the FIFO whenever FIFO 4 meets the FIFO_STA_CFG.LEVEL4.LEVEL condition.

This trigger is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=3)</description>
              <bitRange>[27:27]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_LEVEL5</name>
              <description>FIFO Level 5 Trigger

This level sensitive trigger is set by the FIFO whenever FIFO 5 meets the FIFO_STA_CFG.LEVEL5.LEVEL condition.

This trigger is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=3)</description>
              <bitRange>[28:28]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_LEVEL6</name>
              <description>FIFO Level 6 Trigger

This level sensitive trigger is set by the FIFO whenever FIFO 6 meets the FIFO_STA_CFG.LEVEL6.LEVEL condition.

This trigger is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=3)</description>
              <bitRange>[29:29]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_LEVEL7</name>
              <description>FIFO Level 7 Trigger

This level sensitive trigger is set by the FIFO whenever FIFO 7 meets the FIFO_STA_CFG.LEVEL7.LEVEL condition.

This trigger is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=3)</description>
              <bitRange>[30:30]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>AC</name>
              <description>Autonomus Controller Trigger

This trigger is set by the Autonomus Controller whenever executing a state with  ACTRLR.TIMER_TABLE_STRUCT.TT_CFG1.INTR_SET=1.</description>
              <bitRange>[31:31]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>INTR</name>
