        <register>
          <name>FIFO_INTR</name>
          <description>FIFO Interrupt request register</description>
          <addressOffset>0x60</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_OVERFLOW0</name>
              <description>FIFO Overflow 0 Interrupt Request

FIFO Overflow 0 Interrupt: hardware sets this interrupt whenever FIFO 0 overflows (i.e. a write to FIFO 0 fails because FIFO 0 is full).

Write a '1' to clear bit.</description>
              <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_OVERFLOW1</name>
              <description>FIFO Overflow 1 Interrupt Request

FIFO Overflow 1 Interrupt: hardware sets this interrupt whenever FIFO 1 overflows (i.e. a write to FIFO 1 fails because FIFO 1 is full).

This interrupt is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=1,2, or 3)  

Write a '1' to clear bit.</description>
              <bitRange>[1:1]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_OVERFLOW2</name>
              <description>FIFO Overflow 2 Interrupt Request

FIFO Overflow 2 Interrupt: hardware sets this interrupt whenever FIFO 2 overflows (i.e. a write to FIFO 2 fails because FIFO 2 is full).

This interrupt is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=2, or 3) 

Write a '1' to clear bit.</description>
              <bitRange>[2:2]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_OVERFLOW3</name>
              <description>FIFO Overflow 3 Interrupt Request

FIFO Overflow 3 Interrupt: hardware sets this interrupt whenever FIFO 3 overflows (i.e. a write to FIFO 3 fails because FIFO 3 is full).

This interrupt is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=2, or 3) 

Write a '1' to clear bit.</description>
              <bitRange>[3:3]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_OVERFLOW4</name>
              <description>FIFO Overflow 4 Interrupt Request

FIFO Overflow 4 Interrupt: hardware sets this interrupt whenever FIFO 4 overflows (i.e. a write to FIFO 4 fails because FIFO 4 is full).

This interrupt is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=3) 

Write a '1' to clear bit.</description>
              <bitRange>[4:4]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_OVERFLOW5</name>
              <description>FIFO Overflow 5 Interrupt Request

FIFO Overflow 5 Interrupt: hardware sets this interrupt whenever FIFO 5 overflows (i.e. a write to FIFO 5 fails because FIFO 5 is full).

This interrupt is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=3) 

Write a '1' to clear bit.</description>
              <bitRange>[5:5]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_OVERFLOW6</name>
              <description>FIFO Overflow 6 Interrupt Request

FIFO Overflow 6 Interrupt: hardware sets this interrupt whenever FIFO 6 overflows (i.e. a write to FIFO 6 fails because FIFO 6 is full).

This interrupt is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=3) 

Write a '1' to clear bit.</description>
              <bitRange>[6:6]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_OVERFLOW7</name>
              <description>FIFO Overflow 7 Interrupt Request

FIFO Overflow 7 Interrupt: hardware sets this interrupt whenever FIFO 7 overflows (i.e. a write to FIFO 7 fails because FIFO 7 is full).

This interrupt is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=3) 

Write a '1' to clear bit.</description>
              <bitRange>[7:7]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_UNDERFLOW0</name>
              <description>FIFO Underflow 0 Interrupt Request

FIFO Underflow 0 Interrupt: hardware sets this interrupt whenever FIFO 0 underflows (i.e. a read from FIFO 0 fails because FIFO 0 is empty.

Write a '1' to clear bit.</description>
              <bitRange>[8:8]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_UNDERFLOW1</name>
              <description>FIFO Overflow 1 Interrupt Request

FIFO Underflow 1 Interrupt: hardware sets this interrupt whenever FIFO 1 underflows (i.e. a read from FIFO 1 fails because FIFO 1 is empty).

This interrupt is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=1,2, or 3)  

Write a '1' to clear bit.</description>
              <bitRange>[9:9]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_UNDERFLOW2</name>
              <description>FIFO Overflow 2 Interrupt Request

FIFO Overflow 2 Interrupt: hardware sets this interrupt whenever FIFO 2 underflows (i.e. a read from FIFO 2 fails because FIFO 2 is empty).

This interrupt is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=2, or 3)  

Write a '1' to clear bit.</description>
              <bitRange>[10:10]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_UNDERFLOW3</name>
              <description>FIFO Overflow 3 Interrupt Request

FIFO Overflow 3 Interrupt: hardware sets this interrupt whenever FIFO 3 underflows (i.e. a read from FIFO 3 fails because FIFO 3 is empty).

This interrupt is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=2, or 3)  

Write a '1' to clear bit.</description>
              <bitRange>[11:11]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_UNDERFLOW4</name>
              <description>FIFO Overflow 4 Interrupt Request

FIFO Overflow 4 Interrupt: hardware sets this interrupt whenever FIFO 4 underflows (i.e. a read from FIFO 4 fails because FIFO 4 is empty).

This interrupt is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=3)  

Write a '1' to clear bit.</description>
              <bitRange>[12:12]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_UNDERFLOW5</name>
              <description>FIFO Overflow 5 Interrupt Request

FIFO Overflow 5 Interrupt: hardware sets this interrupt whenever FIFO 5 underflows (i.e. a read from FIFO 5 fails because FIFO 5 is empty).

This interrupt is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=3)  

Write a '1' to clear bit.</description>
              <bitRange>[13:13]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_UNDERFLOW6</name>
              <description>FIFO Overflow 6 Interrupt Request

FIFO Overflow 6 Interrupt: hardware sets this interrupt whenever FIFO 6 underflows (i.e. a read from FIFO 6 fails because FIFO 6 is empty).

This interrupt is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=3)  

Write a '1' to clear bit.</description>
              <bitRange>[14:14]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_UNDERFLOW7</name>
              <description>FIFO Overflow 7 Interrupt Request

FIFO Overflow 7 Interrupt: hardware sets this interrupt whenever FIFO 7 underflows (i.e. a read from FIFO 7 fails because FIFO 7 is empty).

This interrupt is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=3)  

Write a '1' to clear bit.</description>
              <bitRange>[15:15]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RSVD_0</name>
              <description>N/A</description>
              <bitRange>[16:16]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_LEVEL0</name>
              <description>FIFO Level 0 Interrupt Request

FIFO Level 0 Interrupt: hardware sets this level sensitive interrupt whenever FIFO 0 meets the FIFO_STA_CFG.LEVEL0.LEVEL condition.

This interrupt is only cleared when the contents of FIFO drop below the FIFO_STA_CFG.LEVEL0.LEVEL condition.</description>
              <bitRange>[17:17]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RSVD_1</name>
              <description>N/A</description>
              <bitRange>[19:18]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_LEVEL1</name>
              <description>FIFO Level 1 Interrupt Request

FIFO Level 1 Interrupt: hardware sets this level sensitive interrupt whenever FIFO 1 meets the FIFO_STA_CFG.LEVEL1.LEVEL condition.

This interrupt is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=1,2, or 3) 

This interrupt is only cleared when the contents of FIFO drop below the FIFO_STA_CFG.LEVEL1.LEVEL condition.</description>
              <bitRange>[20:20]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RSVD_2</name>
              <description>N/A</description>
              <bitRange>[24:21]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_LEVEL2</name>
              <description>FIFO Level 2 Interrupt Request

FIFO Level 2 Interrupt: hardware sets this level sensitive interrupt whenever FIFO 2 meets the FIFO_STA_CFG.LEVEL2.LEVEL condition.

This interrupt is only generated if the FIFO is configured for multiple FIFOs (i.e. FIFO_STA_CFG.CFG.SEL=2, or 3)  

This interrupt is only cleared when the contents of FIFO drop below the FIFO_STA_CFG.LEVEL2.LEVEL condition.</description>
              <bitRange>[25:25]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FIFO_LEVEL3</name>
              <description>FIFO Level 3 Interrupt Request

FIFO Level 3 Interrupt: hardware sets this level sensitive interrupt whenever FIFO 3 meets the FIFO_STA_CFG.LEVEL3.LEVEL condition.

