                <bitRange>[28:19]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>PID</name>
                <description>PID (Pid)

The application programs this field with the type of PID to use for the initial transaction. The host maintains this field for the rest of the transfer.
 - 2'b00: DATA0
 - 2'b01: DATA2
 - 2'b10: DATA1
 - 2'b11: MDATA (non-control)/SETUP (control)</description>
                <bitRange>[30:29]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>DATA0</name>
                    <description>DATA0</description>
                    <value>0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>DATA1</name>
                    <description>DATA1</description>
                    <value>2</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>DATA2</name>
                    <description>DATA2</description>
                    <value>1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>MDATA</name>
                    <description>MDATA (non-control)/SETUP (control)</description>
                    <value>3</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>DOPNG</name>
                <description>Do Ping (DoPng)

This bit is used only for OUT transfers.
Setting this field to 1 directs the host to do PING protocol.

Note: Do not set this bit for IN transfers. If this bit is set for for IN transfers it disables the channel.</description>
                <bitRange>[31:31]</bitRange>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>NOPING</name>
                    <description>No ping protocol</description>
                    <value>0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>PING</name>
                    <description>Ping protocol</description>
                    <value>1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>HCDMA2</name>
